<task id="005" project="spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-08: Unwind tactical `maxHeight` hack from 6 sections + set `contentSizing: 'clamped'` in metadata catalog</title>
    <phase>1: Framework Schema + Consumer Unwind</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>1</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>001</dependencies>
    <blocks>006</blocks>
    <tags>frontend, typescript, legal-workspace, section-registrations, multi-file, cleanup</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies 7 `.ts` files across shared lib + solution; multi-file coordinated edit; blocks Phase 1 close</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>Wave 2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    After FR-01 (`contentSizing` framework field) has landed, unwind the tactical `maxHeight: '480px'` + `display: 'flex'` additions from the 6 entity-list section registration files in LegalWorkspace. Simultaneously add `contentSizing: 'clamped'` to the 6 corresponding metadata catalog entries. Consider using parallel subagents for the 6 identical registration edits per CLAUDE.md § Multi-File Work Decomposition.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE frontend framework developer coordinating a multi-file cleanup pass. Uses parallel-subagent decomposition for the 6 identical registration edits.
  </role>

  <goal>
    (a) `sectionMetadataCatalog.ts`: 6 entries have `contentSizing: 'clamped'`. (b) 6 registration files: no `maxHeight`, no `display: 'flex'` in `style` block (framework now provides these via `contentSizing`). (c) Grep confirms zero `maxHeight` in `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/{communications,documents,invoices,matters,projects,workAssignments}.registration.ts`.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The tactical fix deployed 2026-07-01 during `ai-spaarke-ai-workspace-UI-r2` follow-up added `maxHeight: '480px'` to 6 entity-list section registrations to force scrollbars in Dashboard II. This section-level hack violates the "framework decides sizing; sections declare intent" principle and wastes vertical space on single-section full-page layouts (e.g., Documents system layout). FR-01 replaces the hack with `contentSizing: 'clamped'` metadata; FR-08 removes the hack.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/sectionMetadataCatalog.ts</file>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/communications.registration.ts</file>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/documents.registration.ts</file>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/invoices.registration.ts</file>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/matters.registration.ts</file>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/projects.registration.ts</file>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/workAssignments.registration.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Framework metadata lives in shared lib; consumer registrations reference it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Depends on FR-01 (task 001) — do NOT start this before 001 is ✅.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Identical edit pattern across 6 files — good candidate for parallel subagent decomposition.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
